pdfium-render Rust bindings (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
---------------------------------------------
Browsey links pdfium-render 0.9.4, using the explicitly selected pdfium_7881
API profile, thread_safe, and image_025. The bundled 8076 binaries are tested
against this profile; pdfium_latest is not used as an implicit ABI selection.
Included license declaration: `resources/pdfium-render-LICENSE.md`.
Source and license: https://docs.rs/crate/pdfium-render/0.9.4/source/LICENSE.md
License expressions and crate checksum are also recorded in Cargo.lock / the
published crate metadata.

GLib Rust bindings (MIT)
-----------------------
Browsey uses GLib 0.18.5 with the upstream mutable out-pointer fix backported
for RUSTSEC-2024-0429, preserving Tauri's GTK3/GIO ABI. The source, MIT license
and COPYRIGHT are retained under `vendor/glib/`; the packaged MIT license is
`resources/glib-LICENSE`. Provenance is recorded in `vendor/provenance.json`.
Fix: https://github.com/gtk-rs/gtk-rs-core/pull/1343

UnRAR decoder source (UnRAR license)
------------------------------------
Browsey statically links the UnRAR decoder through `unrar_sys` for read-only
RAR extraction. The native decoder is stable UnRAR 7.23, built from source
package revision 7.2.7 (not the source-download beta). Browsey carries a local
unrar_sys 0.5.8 patch with refreshed native source and matching packed FFI
structures. Source hashes and build provenance are in `vendor/provenance.json`.
The Rust bindings are MIT OR Apache-2.0; their full licenses are packaged as
`resources/unrar-sys-LICENSE-MIT` and `resources/unrar-sys-LICENSE-APACHE`.
The native license is included as `resources/unrar-LICENSE.txt`. The decoder source is
distributed under the UnRAR license:

